        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Salamis</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">480 BCE; no day is stated, and the timeline of the battle is difficult to establish with certainty</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The straits between the island of Salamis and the mainland, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saronic-gulf">Saronic Gulf</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Allied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-city-states">Greek city-states</a>, nominally under the Spartan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eurybiades">Eurybiades</a> and effectively under the Athenian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistocles">Themistocles</a>, with 378 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trireme">triremes</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a>'s count (his contingents add up to 371), 310 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeschylus">Aeschylus</a> and 220 by Hyperides; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a>, with 1,207 triremes at the outset by Herodotus, though most modern historians favour 600 to 800 at Salamis</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">A Greek victory. The Persian fleet withdrew to Phalerum, its losses unstated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> and estimated at 200 to 300 ships from his later figures, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xerxes-i">Xerxes</a> retreated to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> with much of his army, leaving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>.</span></div>
        </div>
